    "body": "Fixes #5252.\n\nC tuple truth testing returned false for nonempty tuples and discarded evaluation of the tuple expression. Keep the expression evaluated once before producing its truth value, preserving assignments, function calls and exceptions without converting the tuple to a Python object.\n\nAdds regressions for walrus assignments, evaluation order, short-circuiting and `nogil` calls, and corrects the existing expectation for `not (1, 2)`.\n\nTested C/C++ output on Windows with Python 3.12–3.14, the related tuple/boolean/walrus suite (557 tests), compiler/unit/style checks (292 passed, 1 skipped), and the installed wheel's `cythonize` CLI.\n",
